{"author":{"id":"1832e4168d45d4ef31531146dbc743bb950a5dd543b15fd8e3a076fd976bfdef"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791024136,"nonce":"zXbqfYBs4gTRcL+v9Kt6Tb1oxeo=","title":"HashLink binds an IDL float as f32 while Haxe declares Float, a double","message":"Stock HashLink refuses to load xgpu.hdll:\n\n    FATAL ERROR : Invalid signature for function xgpu@gpu_sampler_descriptor_lod_max_clamp : PXxgpu_GpuSamplerDescriptor_d_v required but PXxgpu_GpuSamplerDescriptor_f_v found in hdll\n\nhx_type maps f32 to Float, which HashLink types as f64 ('d'), while hashlink_signature gives f32 'f' and hashlink_argument/hashlink_return pass a Rust f32. Every float in the WebGPU API hits it. Ash does not check primitive signatures, so only stock HashLink sees it.\n\nRayzor already widens f32 to f64 at its ABI and narrows inside the wrapper; HashLink now does the same, so the Haxe surface stays Float.","files":null}]}